OpenMinis
---------

Portions of the screen-reading (accessibility) bridge are adapted from OpenMinis,
https://github.com/OpenMinis/OpenMinis, which is licensed under the GNU General
Public License, version 3.

Adapted files and their origin:

  app/src/main/java/com/zhousl/aether/data/accessibility/QingAccessibilityService.kt
      from src/android/app/src/main/java/com/openminis/app/accessibility/MinisAccessibilityService.kt
  app/src/main/java/com/zhousl/aether/data/accessibility/NodeRegistry.kt
      from src/android/app/src/main/java/com/openminis/app/accessibility/NodeRegistry.kt
  app/src/main/res/xml/qing_accessibility_service.xml
      from src/android/app/src/main/res/xml/minis_accessibility_service.xml

What Qing changed:

  - NodeRegistry additionally records the package and window a handle came from, and
    reports a handle as stale when the foreground screen has moved on, instead of only
    expiring it on a timer.
  - The service drops the event ring, screenshot capture and pinch gestures, and no
    longer depends on OpenMinis' recovery manager or logger.
  - The service configuration requests fewer capabilities: no canTakeScreenshot and no
    touch-exploration flag.

The command-line offload layer that OpenMinis wraps around its accessibility service is
NOT ported: it depends on a PRoot-based native offload extension (PRoot is GPLv2-only and
incompatible with this project's licence). Qing talks to its own tool channel instead, and
deliberately does not reproduce that layer's habit of reporting a tap as successful without
checking whether it happened.


